<section id="ranking">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Full ranking</p>
        <h2>The full ranked list.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="sub">Eight findings, in the order to look at them. Findings are ordered first by observed impact, then by strength of evidence. Estimated financial upside is never used.</p>
    </div>
    <span class="sd-tag">Synthetic sample</span>
    <table class="sd-rank">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">#</th><th scope="col">Finding</th><th scope="col">Confidence</th><th scope="col">Impact</th><th scope="col">Next step</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="c-n">1</td><td class="c-f">Contracts waiting on lender funding</td><td class="c-c">Confirmed</td><td class="c-i">High</td><td class="c-x">Deal Flow Investigation</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c-n">2</td><td class="c-f">Missed calls with no recorded callback</td><td class="c-c">Strong signal</td><td class="c-i">High</td><td class="c-x">Implementation scoping</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c-n">3</td><td class="c-f">After-hours leads with no owner</td><td class="c-c">Strong signal</td><td class="c-i">High</td><td class="c-x">Deal Flow Investigation</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c-n">4</td><td class="c-f">Aging items in the accounting schedule</td><td class="c-c">Strong signal</td><td class="c-i">High</td><td class="c-x">Implementation scoping</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c-n">5</td><td class="c-f">Leads matched to a vehicle that sold</td><td class="c-c">Likely</td><td class="c-i">High</td><td class="c-x">Deal Flow Investigation</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c-n">6</td><td class="c-f">Provider A leads with no logged contact</td><td class="c-c">Likely</td><td class="c-i">High</td><td class="c-x">Deal Flow Investigation</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c-n">7</td><td class="c-f">Appointments with no final disposition</td><td class="c-c">Likely</td><td class="c-i">High</td><td class="c-x">Deal Flow Investigation</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c-n">8</td><td class="c-f">Incomplete deal jackets at the pre-delivery gate</td><td class="c-c">Strong signal</td><td class="c-i">Medium</td><td class="c-x">Deal Flow Investigation</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <div class="sd-read">
      <p><b>How to read the order</b></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Why is #8 last? Its impact is Medium, which places it below every High finding even though its evidence is Strong.</li>
        <li>Why is #4 above #5? Within the same impact level, a Strong signal ranks above a Likely one.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><b>Two terms.</b> A Deal Flow Investigation is a deeper look at one journey, such as how a lead becomes a deal. Implementation scoping defines the fix for a store-wide issue.</p>
      <p class="disclaim">Example Motors is built with many stalls so the report can show every part of its format. A real Diagnostic may find fewer, or none.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="anatomy">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Anatomy of a finding</p>
        <h2>Anatomy of a finding.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="sub">Finding #1, in full. Every finding in the report is built the same way.</p>
    </div>
    <span class="sd-tag">Synthetic sample</span>
    <table class="sd-anat">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Finding #1</th><th scope="col">What this part does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">What was observed</th><td>5 of 19 eligible contracts (26.3%) were not funded within the store's 7-day standard. Eligible contracts are those submitted on Days 1 to 7, so each had a full 7 days by Day 14. 3 of the 5 deals are still unposted.</td><td class="cap">Facts only: counts, the store's own standard, and the window.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Observed impact</th><td>$131,700 is unresolved, which is 23.1% of the $571,200 in eligible contracts.</td><td class="cap">Only what the records show. No projections.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Evidence</th><td>The lender portal funding report identifies each contract. The bank deposit report shows no lender deposit for the same five. The deal-status export shows the same deals still open. The F&amp;I manager interview names outstanding stips as the usual cause.</td><td class="cap">Every source is named.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Confidence</th><td><b>Confirmed.</b> The five contracts are identified individually, the counts reproduce from the source records, and an independent source verifies them.</td><td class="cap">The level, and exactly why.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Cause</th><td><b>Waiting.</b> The contracts are waiting on lender conditions that have not been cleared.</td><td class="cap">The kind of stall found.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Business implication</th><td>Unfunded contracts may tie up cash and may leave deals unposted at month-end. No amount is estimated beyond the $131,700 observed.</td><td class="cap">Labeled as interpretation, and kept apart from the facts.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Recommended next step</th><td>A Deal Flow Investigation to trace each of the five contracts to its outstanding condition and to the role that clears it.</td><td class="cap">Diagnose before prescribing.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="coverage">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Coverage</p>
        <h2>Not everything becomes a finding.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="sub">A Diagnostic that only reports problems isn't a diagnostic. Three other outcomes from the same sample.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sd-cards">
      <article class="sd-card">
        <span class="sd-tag">Synthetic sample</span>
        <h3>No signal found.</h3>
        <p class="sd-meta">Appointment Confirmation &amp; Recovery.</p>
        <p>59 of 64 appointments (92.2%) had a logged confirmation the day before, against the store's 90% target. The Diagnostic found no credible signal. That does not show the workflow is working well.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="sd-card">
        <span class="sd-tag">Synthetic sample</span>
        <h3>Not enough evidence.</h3>
        <p class="sd-meta">Trade Appraisal Handoff.</p>
        <p>Suspected but not confirmed. A blank appraisal field on 7 of 31 deals could mean a missing appraisal or an unlinked one. What would settle it: an export from the appraisal tool with timestamps.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="sd-card">
        <span class="sd-tag">Synthetic sample</span>
        <h3>Not assessed at Store depth.</h3>
        <p class="sd-meta">Desk Queue Wait.</p>
        <p>Assessing it needs live desking data. It is left for a deeper look and is not guessed at.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="sd-line">None of these is read as a clean result.</p>
  </div>
</section>

